{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q2377382","formula":"CH₃NO","hill":"CH3NO","elements":["H","C","N","O"],"composition":{"C":1.0,"H":3.0,"N":1.0,"O":1.0},"names":{"en":"Oxaziridine","uk":"Оксазиридин"},"descriptions":{"en":"An oxaziridine is an organic molecule that features a three-membered heterocycle containing oxygen, nitrogen, and carbon. In their largest industrial application, oxaziridines are intermediates in the production of hydrazine. Oxaziridine derivatives are also used as specialized organic chemistry reagents for a variety of enantioselective oxidations and aminations.","uk":"Оксазиридини (англ. oxaziridines) — хімічні сполуки, що містять у молекулі тричленний насичений гетероцикл, в який входять атоми O та N. Легко зазнають гомолітичного розриву зв'язку O–N, через що можуть використовуватися як ініціатори радикальної полімеризації."},"fame":17,"pubchemCid":15817734,"mass":45.041,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1NO1","inchikey":"SJGALSBBFTYSBA-UHFFFAOYSA-N","iupac":"oxaziridine","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"15817734","atoms":6,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-0.365,"y":0.743,"z":0.0,"el":"O"},{"x":0.839,"y":-0.062,"z":0.0,"el":"N"},{"x":-0.474,"y":-0.681,"z":0.0,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.772,"y":-1.165,"z":-0.919,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.77,"y":-1.175,"z":0.915,"el":"H"},{"x":1.163,"y":0.11,"z":0.951,"el":"H"}],"bonds":[[0,1,1],[0,2,1],[1,2,1],[1,5,1],[2,3,1],[2,4,1]]},"sources":[{"role":"identity","name":"Wikidata","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q2377382","license":"CC0 1.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (en)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oxaziridine","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0"},{"role":"description","name":"Wikipedia (uk)","url":"https://uk.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%9E%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B0%D0%B7%D0%B8%D1%80%D0%B8%D0%B4%D0%B8%D0%BD","license":